    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d607-a7">

                <pb facs="0682" n="602" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg602"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 7.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Powell to Commander Nickels.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-05-29"><hi rendition="#italic">May 29,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge your favor
                    of this date requesting to be informed of the status of Vice-Admiral Killick and
                    the two Haitian gunboats, in order that you may be governed in your future
                    intercourse with them.</p>
                <p>In reply I have the honor to state that Vice-Admiral Killick represents the
                    marine arm of the Provisional Government recently established and recognized by
                    the diplomatic agents accredited to this Government. Such being the case, I deem
                    it to be proper to request that their vessel or vessels join with us in the
                    celebration of that national holiday that is cherished by us in commemorating
                    the memory of those who gave their lives in defense of their country’s flag.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. F. Powell.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
